  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through next Friday)\nIssued at 1154 PM CDT Thu May 28 2026\n\nAn unsettled weather pattern will persist through much of the \nlong term with a persistent weak-moderate upper level west-\nsouthwest flow with a few disturbances moving across our area \nthrough next week. Also, a surface dryline will be located to our \nwest late this weekend and early next week. There will be moderate\ninstability and abundant moisture in the area but lift will be \nweak through the long term. The severe weather chances look low at\nthis time, but can not rule out an isolated strong to marginal \nsevere storm, especially Saturday evening across northern areas \nalong the dryline. Going with mainly low to medium chances of rain\nthrough much of the long term, mainly Tuesday through Thursday \nwith isolated to scattered afternoon and evening showers and \nthunderstorms. Most areas will see little rainfall through the \nlong term. Expect hot conditions this weekend with highs in the \n90s, around 100 northwest Big Country Sunday, cooling back into \nthe 80s by the middle of next week.",
